WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.248
This lesson covers all ten narrative sections in school 4B. De-escalation is a communication strategy that may create time and choice; it cannot guarantee that a dangerous situation becomes safe.
本课覆盖学校4B全部十节叙述内容。降级沟通是一种可能创造时间和选择的沟通策略，但不能保证危险情境一定变安全。

00:00:13.248 --> 00:00:22.320
We will keep three questions separate: what might be medically wrong, what the behavior means to this person, and what is safe for the team to do next.
我们把三个问题分开：患者可能发生什么医学问题；这些行为对患者本人意味着什么；团队下一步能安全做什么。

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:40.752
A patient who is agitated may be experiencing a time-critical medical problem. Begin with safety and an immediate impression, then look for onset, breathing, temperature, injury, glucose risk, substances, medications and other causes within your assessment and scope.
躁动患者可能正经历时间敏感的医学急症。先保障安全并快速观察，再按评估范围留意起病时间、呼吸、体温、损伤、血糖风险、物质使用、药物及其他原因。

00:00:40.752 --> 00:00:54.768
Do not force a choice between “medical” and “behavioral.” A medical condition can change behavior, and fear or trauma can coexist with illness. Reassess when the story or observations change.
不要把情况硬分成“医学”或“行为”。医学疾病会改变行为，恐惧或创伤也可与疾病并存。病史或观察改变时要重新评估。

00:00:54.768 --> 00:01:07.512
Start with the whole scene, not a facial expression alone. Note movement, speech, breathing, objects, crowding and exits. Compare with what was known before you approached.
先看整体现场，不能只看一种表情。留意动作、言语、呼吸、物品、拥挤及出口，并与接近前的已知情况比较。

00:01:07.512 --> 00:01:21.864
Interpret the observations as working possibilities. Distress and an active threat can coexist; a quiet patient can also have an urgent medical problem. One category does not cancel the other questions.
把观察解释为暂定可能性。痛苦与实际威胁可以共存；安静患者也可能有紧急医学问题。一个类别不能取消其他评估问题。

00:01:21.864 --> 00:01:38.496
Choose the next action that fits the actual conditions. Safe conversation may permit a focused question; an uncontrolled threat may require distance and support before contact. Do not use a risk label as an automatic treatment or detention order.
下一行动应适合实际条件。安全对话可允许重点提问；未控制威胁则可能要求先拉开距离及取得支持，再接触。风险标签不是自动治疗或拘留命令。

00:01:38.496 --> 00:01:50.736
Then check what changed. Increased space may help, have no effect or reveal a new problem. Reassessment tests the plan instead of assuming a technique worked because you used the right words.
随后检查变化。增加空间可能有帮助、无效，或显露新问题。复评是检验计划，而不是因为用了正确词语就认定技巧有效。

00:01:50.736 --> 00:02:07.536
A sudden behavioral change, altered awareness, abnormal breathing, collapse or extreme heat should raise medical concern. No single observation identifies the cause, so combine history, focused exam and repeated vital signs as safe.
突然的行为变化、意识改变、呼吸异常、倒地或极端高热都应提高医学警觉。单一观察无法确定病因，应在安全前提下结合病史、重点检查及重复生命体征。

00:02:07.536 --> 00:02:26.640
The school outline uses the phrase “Excited Delirium.” Treat that as its syllabus wording only. Current teaching should describe observable severe agitation and possible hyperactive delirium, identify causes, and avoid using the phrase as a stand-alone diagnosis.
学校纲要使用“Excited Delirium”一词。只把它视为课程原文。现行教学应描述可观察到的严重躁动和可能的高活动性谵妄，寻找原因，避免把该词当作独立诊断。

00:02:26.640 --> 00:03:02.016
Organize the oxygen chain into four functions: neural/chemical control of breathing, the mechanical work of moving air, gas exchange and transport, and distribution of pulmonary blood flow. Brain or depressant-drug effects can impair drive; muscle weakness, trauma or airway obstruction can impair movement. Alveoli need ventilation and blood flow, and the blood needs adequate hemoglobin and circulation. A behavioral change can therefore be a sign of a delivery problem, not automatically a primary psychiatric symptom.
氧输送链可按四种功能组织：神经化学呼吸控制、移动空气的机械功、气体交换及运输、肺血流分配。脑或抑制药可影响驱动，肌无力、创伤或气道梗阻可影响运动；肺泡需通气和血流，血液也需足够血红蛋白及循环。因此行为变化可能提示输送问题，并不自动是原发精神科症状。

00:03:02.016 --> 00:03:45.000
Hypoxemia concerns low arterial oxygen, whereas tissue hypoxia concerns inadequate oxygen delivery or use. SpO2 estimates a hemoglobin saturation; PaO2 means arterial oxygen partial pressure and reflects dissolved oxygen. Neither directly measures the whole delivery chain. A person with severe anemia or poor circulation may have a plausible saturation but insufficient oxygen delivery. Blood gas analysis also informs carbon dioxide and acid-base status; it is not a single saturation test. Do not rank SpO2 as universally superior for determining oxygen content without considering hemoglobin.
低氧血症涉及动脉氧偏低，组织缺氧涉及氧输送或利用不足。SpO2估计血红蛋白饱和度，PaO2测溶解氧分压，均不直接测整个输送链。严重贫血或循环差者可有看似合理饱和度，却供氧不足。血气还反映二氧化碳及酸碱，并非单一饱和度测试。不能不考虑血红蛋白就把SpO2排为判断含氧量的普遍优胜指标。

00:03:45.000 --> 00:04:18.288
AVPU describes the response you actually elicited: alert, response to voice, response only to an appropriate painful stimulus, or unresponsive. Record the stimulus, response and time, not just sleepy or confused. Alertness does not prove full orientation or decision-making capacity, and response to voice is not equivalent to a normal neurologic assessment. Use approved techniques without repeated unnecessary painful stimulation, then look for a changing trend.
AVPU描述实际诱出的反应：清醒、对声音反应、仅对适当疼痛刺激反应，或无反应。应记刺激、反应及时间，不只写嗜睡或混乱。清醒不证明定向完整或有决策能力，对声音反应也不等同神经检查正常。应采用认可方法，避免反复不必要疼痛刺激，并观察变化趋势。

00:04:18.288 --> 00:04:49.584
The source AVPU table links decreasing responsiveness to airway concern and a semi-prone position when injuries permit. Do not wait for U before assessing breathing or assume every alert person protects the airway despite vomiting, oral bleeding or injury. Positioning depends on airway, breathing, trauma and the actual situation. If ventilation is inadequate, provide the indicated support rather than using a position or one consciousness letter as treatment by itself.
来源AVPU表把反应下降连到气道担忧，并在损伤允许时列半俯卧位。不能等到U才评估呼吸，也不能在呕吐、口腔出血或受伤时默认所有清醒者都能保护气道。体位取决于气道、呼吸、创伤及实际情况。通气不足时应给予有指征支持，不能把某体位或单个意识字母本身当治疗。

00:04:49.584 --> 00:05:06.312
Notice change from baseline and clusters of signs. Pacing may reflect pain, fear, a need to move or a medical problem. Silence may be processing, language access, distrust, exhaustion or a decision not to answer.
观察相对基线的变化和线索组合。踱步可能来自疼痛、恐惧、需要活动或医学问题。沉默可能是在理解、语言障碍、不信任、疲劳，或选择不回答。

00:05:06.312 --> 00:05:19.632
Use neutral language: “The person is pacing, sweating and speaking in short phrases,” not “the person is crazy or dangerous.” Then ask what the person wants and what changed.
使用中性描述：“患者踱步、出汗、说话短促”，不要说“疯了或危险”。随后询问患者想要什么、发生了什么变化。

00:05:19.632 --> 00:05:34.656
If fear is misread as aggression, crowding, commands or premature coercion may intensify distress and damage trust. Silence, averted eyes or a refused question do not establish intent to injure.
把恐惧误读为攻击，可能通过围堵、命令或过早强制加重痛苦并损害信任。沉默、避开眼神或拒答，都不证明伤人意图。

00:05:34.656 --> 00:05:49.248
The opposite error is ignoring specific danger because you want the encounter to remain therapeutic. An assault, weapon or loss of safe egress requires a changed safety plan, not a longer attempt to finish the interview.
相反错误是因为希望维持治疗性互动而忽视具体危险。袭击、武器或安全退出路线丢失，都要求改变安全计划，而不是继续更长访谈。

00:05:49.248 --> 00:06:03.288
A third error is explaining away altered awareness or collapse as bad behaviour. Continue looking for medical causes and new deterioration when assessment becomes safe; do not make the label do the work of an examination.
第三种错误是把意识改变或倒地解释成行为不好。评估安全时应继续寻找医学原因及新发恶化，不能让标签代替检查。

00:06:03.288 --> 00:06:17.568
A useful team statement names the observation, concern and action: The person moved into our exit route; I cannot confirm safe passage; we need space and support. It does not claim certainty about the person’s motive.
有效团队表述会指出观察、担忧及行动：“对方移到了我们的退出通道，我无法确认安全通行，需要空间及支援。”它不宣称已确定对方动机。

00:06:17.568 --> 00:06:31.344
When safe, create space, reduce the audience and remove unnecessary stimulation. Avoid sudden touch, blocking exits, surrounding the patient or making multiple people speak at once.
安全时增加空间、减少围观并降低不必要刺激。避免突然触碰、堵住出口、围住患者或多人同时说话。

00:06:31.344 --> 00:06:42.408
Choose a position that protects both sides and preserves a route to withdraw. Do not enter a confined or unsafe area simply because a calm conversation seems possible.
选择既保护双方又保留撤离路线的位置。不要仅因似乎可以冷静沟通，就进入受限或不安全区域。

00:06:42.408 --> 00:06:56.808
Ask whether sound, light or crowding is making the encounter harder. Reduce unnecessary stimulation where feasible, but do not turn off lighting needed for safe assessment or move into an unsafe secluded space.
询问声音、光线或拥挤是否加重困难。可行时减少无关刺激，但不能关掉安全评估所需照明，也不能移入不安全的偏僻空间。

00:06:56.808 --> 00:07:09.576
Arrange one lead speaker and keep necessary staff connected. Invite unneeded onlookers to create space without escalating a confrontation or pretending you can control every person or camera.
安排一名主要发言者，并保持必要人员联系。可请无关围观者留出空间，但不能升级冲突，也不能假装能控制每个人或每部相机。

00:07:09.576 --> 00:07:23.088
Protect dignity with an explanation, appropriate covering and the minimum exposure required for assessment. Ask about a wanted support person rather than automatically excluding or including all family.
通过解释、适当遮盖及评估所需最少暴露保护尊严。应询问希望哪位支持者在场，而不是自动排除或纳入所有家属。

00:07:23.088 --> 00:07:36.144
Reassess after the change. A quieter environment that blocks an exit, separates the crew or hides breathing is not an improvement. Privacy and safety must be planned together.
改变后重新评估。安静了却堵住出口、使团队分离或看不清呼吸，并非改善。隐私与安全必须一起规划。

00:07:36.144 --> 00:07:48.360
A calm tone is helpful only if your position, pace and actions also feel predictable. Do not imitate the person’s volume, issue rapid commands or make a promise you cannot keep.
冷静语气只有在姿势、节奏及行动同样可预测时才有帮助。不要模仿患者音量、连续快速下命令，或做无法兑现的承诺。

00:07:48.360 --> 00:08:01.728
Cultural humility still applies under pressure. Do not assume eye contact, silence, distance or touch carries the same meaning for everyone. State what you observed and check your interpretation.
压力下仍需保持文化谦逊。不要假设眼神、沉默、距离或触碰对每个人含义相同。说出观察到的现象，并核实自己的理解。

00:08:01.728 --> 00:08:14.304
The school calls the calming influence of a regulated clinician co-regulation. Treat this as a useful communication concept, not a guarantee that your nervous system can control another person’s response.
学校把稳定医护人员可能产生的安定影响称为co-regulation。应把它当作沟通概念，而不是保证自己的神经系统能控制他人反应。

00:08:14.304 --> 00:08:29.616
Notice whether you are talking faster, interrupting or moving abruptly. If safe, pause, ease your own breathing and use a lower, steady voice. Do not tell a patient with breathing difficulty that they simply need to relax.
留意自己是否越说越快、频繁打断或突然动作。安全时暂停、调整自己的呼吸，并用较低而稳定的声音。不能告诉呼吸困难患者只需放松。

00:08:29.616 --> 00:08:41.976
Ask your partner to observe exits and changes while one person leads communication. Agree how a safety concern will be announced so that the patient does not receive competing instructions.
一人主导沟通时，可请搭档观察出口及变化。应约定如何提出安全担忧，避免让患者接收互相冲突的指令。

00:08:41.976 --> 00:08:55.320
If your own frustration is impairing the encounter, acknowledge it to the team and arrange an appropriate change of speaker or support. A professional reset is more useful than trying to win the last word.
若自身沮丧影响互动，应向团队说明，并适当更换发言者或请求支持。专业调整比争取最后一句话更有用。

00:08:55.320 --> 00:09:07.416
Listen without rushing to correct. Empathy can sound like, “This feels frightening and you want more space.” It does not mean agreeing that another person has done something unverified.
先倾听，不急着纠正。共情可以说：“这让你感到害怕，你想要更大的空间。”但这不代表认同未经核实的指控。

00:09:07.416 --> 00:09:18.984
Ask one question at a time. Paraphrase the patient’s priority, then summarize the next step in plain language. Check understanding instead of treating a nod as proof.
一次问一个问题。复述患者最关心的事，再用通俗语言总结下一步。要确认理解，不能把点头直接当作理解的证明。

00:09:18.984 --> 00:09:31.704
Listen for what the person is trying to protect or obtain. A demand to leave may relate to a dependent person, a pet, a job or fear of the service. Ask rather than guessing the reason.
倾听对方想保护或取得什么。要求离开可能涉及需要照顾的人、宠物、工作，或对服务的恐惧。应询问，不能猜原因。

00:09:31.704 --> 00:09:45.840
Allow a thought to finish when the situation permits. A brief pause can be more helpful than immediately adding a solution. Continue observing clinical and scene safety rather than becoming absorbed in one story.
情况允许时，让对方说完一个意思。简短停顿可能比立即给方案更有帮助。同时继续观察临床及现场安全，不能完全陷入一段叙述。

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:58.536
Empathize with the expressed difficulty: It sounds as though not knowing the plan has made this harder. Invite correction. You can acknowledge fear without agreeing that an unverified accusation is true.
可以回应所表达的困难：“听起来，不知道接下来安排什么，让这件事更难受了。”允许纠正。承认恐惧不等于认可未经核实的指控。

00:09:58.536 --> 00:10:10.368
Do not promise a painless procedure, immediate discharge or a particular hospital outcome. Honest support explains what you can do now and what remains outside your control.
不能承诺操作无痛、立即出院或某种医院结果。诚实支持应说明现在能做什么，以及什么仍超出自己的控制。

00:10:10.368 --> 00:10:22.728
An open question gives room for the person’s priority. Once it is clear, use focused questions for the immediate decision. Do not ask a long list simply because it appears on your mental checklist.
开放式问题让本人有机会表达优先事项。清楚后，再用重点问题支持即时决定。不能仅因为脑中有清单，就一口气问一长串。

00:10:22.728 --> 00:10:36.864
Explain the purpose of a potentially sensitive question and ask only what is relevant. For example, an onset question can help distinguish a new change from the person’s usual state without making a judgment about character.
可能敏感的问题应先解释用途，并只问相关内容。例如询问起病时间，可区分新变化与平常状态，而无需评判品格。

00:10:36.864 --> 00:10:48.048
Pause for the answer and use appropriate communication support. Limited English, hearing loss or a long processing pause is not proof of confusion or deliberate resistance.
留出回答时间，并使用适当沟通支持。英语有限、听力下降或处理信息较慢，都不证明意识混乱或故意抵抗。

00:10:48.048 --> 00:11:03.048
Urgent medical assessment may need a short direct question rather than a broad conversation. Explain the change in priority. LEAPS organizes communication; it does not require a complete interview before responding to deterioration.
紧急医学评估可能需要简短直接问题，而不是广泛交谈。应解释优先级变化。LEAPS组织沟通，不要求先完成完整访谈才能回应恶化。

00:11:03.048 --> 00:11:13.992
Paraphrasing checks your interpretation of the concern. Use your own words and invite correction: You want to know who will secure the shop before we discuss leaving; have I understood that?
Paraphrase是检查自己对担忧的理解。用自己的话复述并允许纠正：“你想先知道谁来锁好店门，然后再谈离开，我理解得对吗？”

00:11:13.992 --> 00:11:27.288
A summary is broader. It states the concern, the immediate assessment or support step, any genuine choice and what remains unresolved. It is not merely repeating the patient’s last sentence.
Summary范围更广，整合担忧、即时评估或支持步骤、真实选择及未解决事项。它不是只重复患者最后一句话。

00:11:27.288 --> 00:11:40.272
Do not insert an agreement that was never given. We have discussed checking your breathing is different from You agreed to transport. A response to one proposal does not automatically authorize the next procedure.
不能加进对方从未作出的同意。“我们讨论过检查呼吸”不同于“你同意转运”。回应一项提议，不会自动授权下一操作。

00:11:40.272 --> 00:11:50.976
If the summary is corrected, update the plan rather than defending your wording. The useful result is a shared next step, or a clear description of what is still disputed.
若对方纠正总结，应更新计划，而不是维护自己的措辞。有用结果是双方理解下一步，或清楚说明什么仍有分歧。

00:11:50.976 --> 00:12:06.672
In this original case, a shopkeeper says everyone must leave and repeatedly looks toward an unlocked rear door. From a safe position, ask the main concern. They say a cash drawer and customer property would be left unsecured.
原创案例中，店主要求所有人离开，并反复看向未上锁的后门。从安全位置询问主要担忧后，对方说现金抽屉及顾客物品会无人看管。

00:12:06.672 --> 00:12:19.800
Acknowledge the concern without assuming it explains every symptom: Leaving those items unsecured is worrying you. Ask whether there is a person they want contacted while the immediate clinical assessment is discussed.
承认担忧，但不假定它解释全部症状：“这些东西无人看管，让你很担心。”再询问讨论即时临床评估时，是否希望联系某位支持者。

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:31.224
Paraphrase the actual request and confirm permission before contacting anyone. Do not search the premises, handle money or promise police attendance as an improvised reassurance.
复述真实请求，并在联系他人前确认许可。不能为了临时安慰而搜查店铺、处理现金，或承诺警察到场。

00:12:31.224 --> 00:12:45.864
Summarize the feasible next step and its limit. If new clinical danger appears, explain that priority and obtain the indicated support. A resolved practical concern is not proof that medical risk has resolved.
总结可行下一步及局限。若出现新临床危险，应解释优先级并取得所需支持。实际担忧解决，不代表医学风险也已解决。

00:12:45.864 --> 00:12:56.256
A choice is not meaningful if both options are unsafe or the decision has already been made without explanation. Offer only options you can honor, then follow through.
若两个选项都不安全，或决定已在未解释时作出，这种选择就没有意义。只提供你能兑现的选项，并付诸行动。

00:12:56.256 --> 00:13:07.560
When you must set a limit, be brief and concrete. Explain the safety reason, say what you can do, and avoid threats or bargaining about care that is required now.
必须设限时要简短具体。说明安全原因和自己能做什么，避免威胁，也不要拿必须进行的照护作交易。

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:20.064
De-escalation is not a requirement to remain close to an immediate threat. If risk rises, stop the interaction, create distance, communicate the hazard and request the appropriate help.
降级沟通不要求你继续靠近即时威胁。若风险上升，应停止互动、拉开距离、报告危险并请求适当支援。

00:13:20.064 --> 00:13:35.928
Restraint or medication is not an automatic next step. It requires the correct legal/service authority, trained personnel, monitoring and a current protocol. This lesson does not teach hands-on restraint or sedation technique.
约束或用药不是自动的下一步，需要正确的法律/服务授权、受训人员、监测及现行规程。本课不教授徒手约束或镇静技术。

00:13:35.928 --> 00:13:50.640
De-escalation may be failing when dangerous conduct intensifies or safe passage is no longer available. Repeatedly refusing a question is not the same evidence as a specific threat, so describe the actual change.
危险行为加剧或安全通行不再可用时，降级沟通可能已经失败。反复拒答与具体威胁不是相同证据，因此应描述实际变化。

00:13:50.640 --> 00:14:04.032
Do not remain to complete LEAPS, retrieve a replaceable bag or prove that your technique works. Follow the trained egress plan with your partner. Do not improvise a physical confrontation or pursue into danger.
不能为了完成LEAPS、取回可更换的包，或证明技巧有效而留下。应与搭档执行受训退出计划，不能临时发生肢体对抗或追入危险。

00:14:04.032 --> 00:14:19.296
From a safer position, tell dispatch where you are and why patient contact cannot safely continue. Request the appropriate response and communicate any known urgent patient concern. Do not assume somebody else has reported the withdrawal.
到较安全位置后，告知调度自己的位置及不能安全继续接触患者的原因。请求适当响应，并传递已知紧急患者问题。不能假定别人已经报告撤离。

00:14:19.296 --> 00:14:37.440
Continue coordinated responsibility: report, stage, reassess conditions and arrange safe care through the incident response. Withdrawal is not a reason to erase the patient from the plan, and an apparent pause in hostility does not automatically clear re-entry.
仍须维持协调责任：报告、集结、复评条件，并通过事件响应安排安全照护。撤离不能让患者从计划中消失；敌意暂时停顿，也不自动证明可以重新进入。

00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:49.968
The goal is not to win an argument or force cooperation. The goal is to protect life and create a safe path to assessment. Do not promise that a specific responder or legal outcome will occur.
目标不是争论取胜或强迫配合，而是保护生命并创造安全评估条件。不要承诺一定会有某名支援人员到场或出现某种法律结果。

00:14:49.968 --> 00:15:08.112
Under the BC Mental Health Act, section Twenty-Eight, subsection One specifies an apprehension route for a police officer or constable meeting its criteria. Do not teach this as independent PCP detention authority or as the only legal route for all involuntary care.
BC《精神健康法》第28条第1款，为符合条件的警员或治安官规定特定送诊路径。不能把它教成PCP独立拘留权，也不能视为所有非自愿照护唯一合法路径。

00:15:08.112 --> 00:15:21.600
A patient can be distressed and still make a decision. A calm answer also does not prove capacity. Neither a psychiatric label nor refusal gives a clinician a new power to confine the person.
患者可能痛苦，却仍能作决定；平静回答也不证明决定能力。精神科标签或拒绝，都不会给医护人员新增限制人身自由的权力。

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:42.792
Section Twenty-Eight, subsection One of the BC Mental Health Act applies to a police officer or constable satisfied, from observations or received information, that the person is acting in a way likely to endanger their own or others’ safety and apparently has a mental disorder. It is not independent PCP detention authority.
BC《精神健康法》第28条第1款，要求警员或治安官根据观察或所得信息，确信本人行为可能危及自己或他人安全，且看来存在精神障碍。这不是PCP独立拘留权。

00:15:42.792 --> 00:15:58.032
Do not expand that statement into a claim that every lawful involuntary-care situation must begin with the same police route. Other legal processes and emergency-care questions need their own current authority and service consultation.
不能把这句话扩大成所有合法非自愿照护都必须先走相同警察路径。其他法律流程及紧急照护问题，需要各自的现行依据及机构咨询。

00:15:58.032 --> 00:16:14.160
For this lesson, the practical task is to communicate observations, identify the authority question and obtain the appropriate decision. LEAPS is not a consent test, certificate, restraint order or substitute for the current refusal pathway.
本课实际任务是沟通观察、指出权限问题，并取得适当决定。LEAPS不是同意测试、证明书、约束命令，也不能替代现行拒绝照护流程。

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:29.496
Prone positioning, pressure on the chest or neck, inability to see the face, exhaustion and sudden quietness can signal severe danger. A patient becoming still is not proof that the underlying problem has resolved.
俯卧、胸部或颈部受压、看不到面部、疲劳及突然安静都可能提示严重危险。患者不再动不代表根本问题已经解决。

00:16:29.496 --> 00:16:46.776
The Week 10 outline asks learners to recall q5min vital signs and respiratory monitoring for restraint scenarios. Keep that as a school station target; follow the current authorized service protocol and monitor continuously enough to detect deterioration.
第10周纲要要求记住约束情景下每5分钟生命体征及呼吸监测。把它保留为学校站点目标；临床须遵循现行授权规程，并持续充分监测以发现恶化。

00:16:46.776 --> 00:16:59.856
A patient may become quieter because communication helped, because exhaustion increased or because their clinical condition deteriorated. Determine what changed instead of treating quietness as a success measure.
患者安静下来，可能因为沟通有帮助、疲劳增加，或临床状况恶化。应确定改变了什么，不能把安静当作成功指标。

00:16:59.856 --> 00:17:12.672
Keep the face, breathing and response observable within the authorized safety plan. The school’s five-minute vital-sign recall target does not mean waiting five minutes to check a new loss of response.
应在获准安全计划内，使面部、呼吸及反应可被观察。学校每5分钟生命体征的记忆目标，不表示新发无反应后要等5分钟再检查。

00:17:12.672 --> 00:17:29.952
G01 emphasizes medical causes and close monitoring. Its level-specific interventions and consultation requirements are not a general permission to sedate or restrain. This lesson does not supply a physical restraint technique or medication dose.
G01强调医学原因及密切监测。其按执业级别列出的干预与咨询要求，不是一般性镇静或约束许可。本课不提供肢体约束手法或药物剂量。

00:17:29.952 --> 00:17:44.712
During transfer, report the observed behaviour and clinical trend, what was attempted, any intervention time and the response. Avoid summarizing the entire event as calmed down when the team needs to know about deterioration.
转交时报告观察到的行为及临床趋势、尝试过什么、干预时间及反应。团队需要知道恶化时，不能把整件事只概括成“冷静下来了”。

00:17:44.712 --> 00:17:59.112
A person at a transit terminal is pacing and shouting. A crowd is filming. The person becomes unsteady and stops speaking. The new quietness changes the problem; it is not an invitation to wait for calm.
一名患者在交通枢纽踱步喊叫，围观者正在拍摄。患者随后步态不稳并停止说话。突然安静改变了问题，不能因此等待“冷静”。

00:17:59.112 --> 00:18:12.264
Move the crowd back if safe, assign one communicator, maintain an exit, check for immediate medical threats and summon appropriate support. Do not approach alone or use the school label as a diagnosis.
安全时请围观者后退，指定一名沟通者，保留撤离路线，检查即时医学威胁并请求合适支援。不要独自接近，也不要用课程术语作诊断。

00:18:12.264 --> 00:18:26.352
Labels can hide medical causes, intensify stigma and reduce the usefulness of a handover. Record direct observations, the person’s words when relevant, time course, interventions and response.
标签会掩盖医学病因、加重污名并降低交接信息价值。应记录直接观察、相关原话、时间经过、干预及反应。

00:18:26.352 --> 00:18:38.160
A concise report says what you see, what you are concerned about, what has been tried and what help is needed. State uncertainty honestly and update the report as the patient changes.
简明报告说明观察到什么、担忧什么、已尝试什么及需要何种帮助。诚实说明不确定性，并随患者变化更新报告。

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:50.856
Record observable behaviour, relevant words, clinical findings, attempted communication and the reason for a changed plan. Separate what you saw from another person’s report and from your interpretation.
记录可观察行为、相关原话、临床发现、沟通尝试及改变计划的原因。应把亲眼观察、他人报告及自己的解释分开。

00:18:50.856 --> 00:19:04.584
After withdrawal, include the communication and staging timeline, resources requested and the unresolved patient risk. Do not retrospectively invent a threat or a refusal to make the record sound tidier.
撤离后应包括沟通及集结时间线、请求资源及未解决患者风险。不能事后编造威胁或拒绝，让记录显得更整齐。

00:19:04.584 --> 00:19:20.424
In the operational review, compare the expected and actual effects of one action. If multiple voices worsened confusion, a practical improvement is one designated speaker and a partner safety role, not a vague promise to be calmer.
行动复盘中，对比一项行动的预期与实际效果。若多人讲话加重混乱，实际改进是一名指定发言者及搭档安全观察职责，而不是笼统承诺更冷静。

00:19:20.424 --> 00:19:35.976
Use the applicable safety-reporting, supervisor and support pathways. An operational debrief does not require personal trauma disclosure and is not confidential therapy. Check readiness and equipment before returning to duty.
使用适用安全报告、主管及支持路径。行动复盘不要求披露私人创伤，也不是保密治疗。重新履职前应检查状态及设备。

00:19:35.976 --> 00:19:49.608
Use the course term “Excited Delirium” only when referring to the school syllabus or an older source. In patient care and documentation, describe the observed signs and use current service language.
提及学校大纲或旧资料时，才使用课程原词“Excited Delirium”。在患者照护和记录中，应描述实际体征并使用现行服务语言。

00:19:49.608 --> 00:20:02.832
This lesson prepares your reasoning and communication. It does not qualify you to restrain, detain, sedate or administer medication outside your legal authority, training and current service policy.
本课帮助准备临床推理与沟通，不会赋予你超出法律权限、培训及现行服务政策的约束、拘留、镇静或给药资格。
